HOLTrace build: Parse strings and make install-worker importable

Scope: build time for recording and replay. The import and worker-pool
changes are also used by the standalone recording-side hashtt rewriter.

The hashtt rewriter adds a `_` argument to constructor patterns with one
comma, e.g. Comb(f,x) -> Comb(f,x,_). It counted commas inside string
literals, so Const(",",_) was left with two arguments and the build
failed (HOL Light Library/words.ml, s2n-bignum common/relational.ml and
others). The tokenizer now reads a string literal as a single token.

The main section is guarded by `if __name__ == '__main__'` so that the
rewriting functions can be imported, and the worker pool uses fork:
with spawn (the macOS default) every worker re-ran the main section.

Trusted-base impact: `install-worker` constructs the HOLTrace wrappers
loaded by the replay build, so it is part of the trusted build path.
The tokenizer, main guard and worker-pool code do not execute while a
trace is replayed and do not modify `fusion.ml`. The hashtt-rewritten
proof and s2n-bignum sources are used only for recording and are outside
the trusted base.

--- a/install-worker
+++ b/install-worker
@@ -59,7 +59,22 @@

 def process(x):
   W = [['','']]
-  for c in x:
+  i = 0
+  while i < len(x):
+    c = x[i]
+    i += 1
+    # A string literal is one token, so that commas and parentheses inside
+    # it are not counted: Const(",",_) has two arguments, not three.
+    # A '"' between single quotes is a character literal, not a string.
+    if c == '"' and not (x[i-2:i-1] == "'" and x[i:i+1] == "'"):
+      j = i
+      while j < len(x) and x[j] != '"':
+        j += 2 if x[j] == '\\' else 1
+      if W[-1] != ['','']:
+        W += [['','']]
+      W[-1][0] += x[i-1:j+1]
+      i = j+1
+      continue
     if c.isalpha():
       if len(W[-1][1]) > 0 or (len(W[-1][0]) > 0 and not W[-1][0].isalpha()):
         W += [['','']]
